Semantic check per changed page: each Plotly.newPlot call's layout and config equal; each trace's x
(the base's array, the candidate's x0 + i * dx) and y bitwise equal; every other trace key equal; the data
argument's text byte-identical once every x array and x0/dx is removed; the page text outside the data
arguments byte-identical. Its teeth, checked on plot-elevator_step-health/health.html: a dx nudged by
1e-7 relative gives 'x differs', a renamed trace gives 'other keys differ' and 'data text differs', and one
added space outside the data gives 'page text outside the data arguments differs'.
Series that fell back to an explicit x (amendment 3), on the elevator_step, 60 s and 300 s logs: none of
the shipped YAML series (every one wrote x0/dx, above). The template's function package ground_track
(trace v0, x = east) keeps its array, as D1 says, and its pages are byte-identical. T2's real rate groups:
divisor 10 rebuilds t bitwise (x0/dx), and divisor 50 does not (explicit x).

